CHAPTER TWO
ENTERPRISE DESIGN AND PROJECT PLANNING
2.0 Introduction
Following the locality analysis conducted in Chapter One, the Agriculture candidates identified improved indigenous (Kienyeji) chicken broiler production as the most suitable livestock enterprise for implementation at St. Mary's Girls Secondary School – Thigio. The enterprise was selected because it responds directly to the major challenges affecting poultry farmers in the locality, namely high feed costs, disease outbreaks, water scarcity, climate variability, and fluctuating market prices.
The project was designed as a climate-smart poultry production enterprise aimed at producing quality indigenous chicken meat while providing learners with practical skills in poultry management, agribusiness, record keeping, and entrepreneurship.
